**What this does**  
1.  In the `useContainer` check, we add  
    ```js
      target.__ol_layer__ === this.getLayer()
    ```  
    so that a container will only be recycled if it was explicitly created by *this* layer, never if it belongs to a different layer that just happened to have the same opacity and transform.  
2.  When we create a brand-new container we write  
    ```js
    container.__ol_layer__ = this.getLayer();
    ```  
    so future calls know “this container is my own.”

With those two tiny changes, two different tile layers each get their own `<canvas>` and the clear/draw sequence works properly even if you give them identical opacities.
